%% apps/hr-service/src/guards. Domain checks depend on the selected endpoint.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant G as API Gateway :3000
    participant S as Protected domain service
    participant A as Auth Service :3001
    participant D as Auth MySQL
    C->>G: API request + Bearer accessToken + optional X-Company-Id
    G->>G: Apply gateway policy
    G->>S: Proxy request with signed client context
    S->>S: JwtAuthGuard: verify HS256, issuer, audience, expiry, type and sid
    S->>A: GET /api/v1/auth/me with bearer token and company header
    A->>A: Verify access JWT
    A->>D: Load active user, current roles and live session by sub + sid
    D-->>A: User and unrevoked, unexpired session
    A->>A: Reject inactive user, required password change or missing MFA assurance
    opt X-Company-Id supplied
        A->>D: Check active membership for INTERNAL user
        D-->>A: Company, branch IDs and permissions
    end
    A-->>S: Current identity, roles and companyScope
    S->>S: Apply endpoint user-type, role and domain permission checks
    Note over S: HR additionally enforces company / branch or employee permissions and ownership
    S-->>G: Authorized result
    G-->>C: Response
    Note over S,A: Invalid session: 401; denied company/permissions: 403.<br/>Auth lookup timeout/unavailability: 503; request is denied.
    Note over C,A: Direct auth endpoints validate against MySQL locally.<br/>They do not call /auth/me recursively.
